      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Steven pays per room by the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. **Identify the given values:**\n   - Amount paid per room: \\(\\frac{11}{2}\\) dollars\n   - Number of rooms cleaned: \\(\\frac{7}{3}\\)\n\n2. **Set up the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total amount owed} = \\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the numerators and denominators separately:**\n   - Numerators: \\(11 \\times 7 = 77\\)\n   - Denominators: \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\)\n\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{77}{6}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify if possible:**\n   The fraction \\(\\frac{77}{6}\\) is already in its simplest form because 77 and 6 have no common factors other than 1.\n\nTherefore, the amount Steven owes Jeremy is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{77}{6}}\\) dollars.",
